amitié si tendre,” and Cyrano promises to protect Christian and be his friend.\",\"supports\":\"Identifies the affection as friendship and places the utterance as grateful acknowledgment rather than a new undertaking.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Roxane has already said of Christian, “Enfin, je l'aime,” and later tells Cyrano, “Nous sommes de grands amis !”\",\"supports\":\"Distinguishes her romantic love for Christian from her friendly affection toward Cyrano.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The utterance begins with “Oh !” but there is no narration that Roxane blurts the words involuntarily or speaks before reflection.\",\"supports\":\"Emotional coloring is present, but the passage supplies no independent evidence for expressive/reflexive core force.\",\"confidence\":0.95}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the avowal of friendly affection. Gratitude, dramatic irony, and emotional coloring belong to contextual interpretation and create no residual pressure beyond T/P/E.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"The nearby second occurrence should not be conflated with the highlighted exact match at the start of “je vous aime bien.”\"}"
